; Registers the .rsproj project type (docs/RSPROJ.md §3, work package 3), key for key the way the
; JavaScript project system registers .esproj in its own Microsoft.VisualStudio.JavaScript.ProjectSystem.pkgdef:
; the project factory itself is the Common Project System's ("ProjectFactoryPackage" = CPS's package),
; "Package" is the package owning the project type (KubunoPackage), and "Capabilities" are the
; capabilities known before the project is even evaluated (the evaluated ones come from
; Kubuno.Rust.Sdk's ProjectCapability items). The GUID is Kubuno.Rust.Sdk's DefaultProjectTypeGuid,
; which is also what a .sln records for a .rsproj.
; A static pkgdef rather than [ProjectTypeRegistration] (Microsoft.VisualStudio.ProjectSystem.VS.dll)
; because, like the JS project system, it keeps the VSIX's CreatePkgDef step free of loading CPS's
; VS-install-only assemblies.
[$RootKey$\Projects\{6C7C4CB5-6E36-4C6F-9C6F-9C6E9B4D4C13}]
@="ProjectFactory"
"ProjectFactoryPackage"="{3347bee8-d7a1-4082-95e4-38a439553cc2}"
"Package"="{5f3a9b2e-9e0c-4f0a-9a7a-6f0f3c9c9d10}"
"DisplayName"="Rust Project"
"DisplayProjectFileExtensions"="Rust Project Files (*.rsproj);*.rsproj"
"DefaultProjectExtension"="rsproj"
"PossibleProjectExtensions"="rsproj"
"Capabilities"="RustProjectSystem;OpenProjectFile;HandlesOwnReload;ProjectConfigurationsDeclaredAsItems;ProjectPropertiesEditor;ProjectPropertyInterception;ConfigurableFileNesting;DynamicFileNesting;DynamicFileNestingEnabled;DynamicDependentFile;NoGeneralDependentFileIcon"
"Language(VsTemplate)"="Rust"
"PrefetchFactory"="{3998970a-aee1-4216-a54f-0a99d20a1fab}"
"ProjectTemplatesDir"="$PackageFolder$\ProjectTemplates"

; docs/RSPROJ.md Addendum (lot 7): "Create a new project"/"Add New Item" templates. The
; Microsoft.VisualStudio.ProjectTemplate/ItemTemplate VSIX asset types alone (source.extension.vsixmanifest)
; get the .vstemplate files copied/cataloged into the VSIX and even generate a .vstman manifest at build
; time, but do NOT make "Create a new project" discover them - verified live: InstalledTemplates.json
; (%LocalAppData%\...\<hive>\InstalledTemplates.json, the actual list the dialog's search index is built
; from) never gained a Kubuno/Rust entry no matter how many times the extension/template caches were
; cleared and rebuilt (devenv /updateconfiguration, deleting ProjectTemplatesCache_.../
; ItemTemplatesCache_.../ComponentModelCache, a real VSIXInstaller install instead of the debug
; DeployExtension copy). What actually wires a template folder in is this NewProjectTemplates\TemplateDirs
; registration (project templates) and the Projects\{guid}\AddItemTemplates\TemplateDirs one (item
; templates) - the same mechanism msbuildproj.pkgdef (CommonExtensions\Microsoft\Project\msbuildproj.pkgdef,
; installed VS 2026's own generic CPS project registration) uses for its own "CPS Projects"/"My Items"
; buckets, read directly off disk from this VS install to find the exact key/value shape. Slot "/2" below
; (msbuildproj.pkgdef's own generic CPS entry already occupies "/1" under the same ProjectFactoryPackage
; GUID - both coexist); "ProjectTemplatesDir" above is kept too since it is the same value
; msbuildproj.pkgdef itself sets redundantly alongside its own NewProjectTemplates entry.
[$RootKey$\NewProjectTemplates\TemplateDirs\{3347bee8-d7a1-4082-95e4-38a439553cc2}\/2]
@="Rust Projects"
"SortPriority"=dword:00000064
"TemplatesDir"="$PackageFolder$\ProjectTemplates"

[$RootKey$\Projects\{6C7C4CB5-6E36-4C6F-9C6F-9C6E9B4D4C13}\AddItemTemplates\TemplateDirs\{3347bee8-d7a1-4082-95e4-38a439553cc2}\/1]
@="Rust Items"
"SortPriority"=dword:00000064
"TemplatesDir"="$PackageFolder$\ItemTemplates"
